⍝ lib/th_piece.imo — spec notation — trusted prelude — generated by libsrc/build.sh from libsrc/th_piece.hum.imo: edit that file, not this one
⍝ th_piece.hum.imo -- the package piecewise: abs, min, max and sgn (human notation; lib/th_piece.imo is its translation, made by libsrc/build.sh).
⍝ The cases are lifted out of the arithmetic: abs(x) is ite(x >= 0, x, -x), a sum or a product with an ite is an ite of sums or products, a relation with an ite is an ite of relations.  What is left is a Boolean
⍝ skeleton over linear (or polynomial) relations, which the diagrams and the elimination of lib/fm.imo decide path by path.
thpiecewisesig ∶ (𝔏 𝕊)
thpiecewisesig ≔ (lines "fn 0 abs abs\nfn 0 max max\nfn 0 min min\nfn 0 sgn sgn")
thpiecewiserules ∶ (𝔏 𝕊)
thpiecewiserules ≔ (lines "abs(x) ==> ite(x >= 0, x, -x)\nmax(x, y) ==> ite(x <= y, y, x)\nmin(x, y) ==> ite(x <= y, x, y)\nsgn(x) ==> ite(x > 0, 1, ite(x < 0, -1, 0))\nadd(ite(c, a, b), y) ==> ite(c, add(a, y), add(b, y))\nmul(ite(c, a, b), y) ==> ite(c, mul(a, y), mul(b, y))\nneg(ite(c, a, b)) ==> ite(c, neg(a), neg(b))\nsub(ite(c, a, b), y) ==> ite(c, sub(a, y), sub(b, y))\nsub(y, ite(c, a, b)) ==> ite(c, sub(y, a), sub(y, b))\npow(ite(c, a, b), n) ==> ite(c, pow(a, n), pow(b, n))\nrdiv(ite(c, a, b), y) ==> ite(c, rdiv(a, y), rdiv(b, y))\nrdiv(y, ite(c, a, b)) ==> ite(c, rdiv(y, a), rdiv(y, b))\neq(ite(c, a, b), y) ==> ite(c, eq(a, y), eq(b, y))\nlt(ite(c, a, b), y) ==> ite(c, lt(a, y), lt(b, y))\nlt(y, ite(c, a, b)) ==> ite(c, lt(y, a), lt(y, b))\nle(ite(c, a, b), y) ==> ite(c, le(a, y), le(b, y))\nle(y, ite(c, a, b)) ==> ite(c, le(y, a), le(y, b))")
thpiecewiseaxioms ∶ (𝔏 𝕊)
thpiecewiseaxioms ≔ (lines "abs(x) = x if x ≥ 0 and -x otherwise (the definition)\nmax(x, y) = y if x ≤ y and x otherwise\nmin(x, y) = x if x ≤ y and y otherwise\nsgn(x) = 1 if x > 0, -1 if x < 0, and 0 if x = 0\nthe order of the reals is total, so the cases of a definition are exhaustive and exclusive")
thpiecewisetheorems ∶ (𝔏 𝕊)
thpiecewisetheorems ≔ (lines "abs(x) >= 0\nabs(x) = abs(-x)\nabs(x + y) <= abs(x) + abs(y)\nabs(x) - abs(y) <= abs(x - y)\nabs(x - y) = abs(y - x)\nabs(x)^2 = x^2\nabs(x) < 1 <=> (-1 < x && x < 1)\nabs(x - y) <= 0 <=> x = y\nabs(x) <= y <=> (-y <= x && x <= y)\nmax(x, y) >= x\nmax(x, y) = max(y, x)\nmin(x, y) = min(y, x)\nmin(x, y) <= max(x, y)\nmax(x, y) + min(x, y) = x + y\nmax(x, y) = (x + y + abs(x - y)) / 2\nmin(x, y) = (x + y - abs(x - y)) / 2\nmax(x, max(y, z)) = max(max(x, y), z)\nmin(x, min(y, z)) = min(min(x, y), z)\nmin(x, y) + z = min(x + z, y + z)\nmax(x, y) + z = max(x + z, y + z)\nmax(x, y) <= z <=> (x <= z && y <= z)\nz <= min(x, y) <=> (z <= x && z <= y)\nmin(x, max(x, y)) = x\nmax(x, min(x, y)) = x\nmax(x, x) = x\nsgn(x) * abs(x) = x\nsgn(x) = 1 <=> x > 0\nsgn(x) = -1 <=> x < 0\nsgn(x) = 0 <=> x = 0\nabs(sgn(x)) <= 1\nx <= abs(x)\n-abs(x) <= x")
thpiecewisedoc ∶ 𝕊
thpiecewisedoc ≔ "absolute value, minimum, maximum and sign as definitions by cases: the cases are lifted out of the arithmetic and decided by the diagrams and the linear arithmetic of each path"
thpiecewise ∶ Theory
thpiecewise ≔ (mktheory "piecewise" (∷ "arith" ⊘) ⊘ ⊥ thpiecewisesig thpiecewiserules ⊘ thpiecewiseaxioms thpiecewisetheorems thpiecewisedoc)
